WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:24.036
As each mermaid princess reached her fifteenth birthday, she was allowed to swim to the Upper World.

2
00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:30.514
Before her journey each sister promised to tell the others what she saw the next day.

3
00:00:30.515 --> 00:00:36.354
When the eldest princess turned 15, she spent her time close to shore.

4
00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:43.525
"I lay on a sandbar in the moonlight and gazed at a distant town," she told her sisters.

5
00:00:43.526 --> 00:00:46.437
"The houses' lights twinkled like stars.

6
00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:51.088
Bells rang from a large house with a tall tower."

7
00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:56.110
The next year the second sister came up to the surface at sunset.

8
00:00:56.111 --> 00:01:00.984
"The sky and the water glowed gold and red," she said.

9
00:01:00.985 --> 00:01:04.946
"I saw fluffy, purple clouds high overhead.

10
00:01:04.947 --> 00:01:11.017
A flock of white swans flew just above the water toward the setting sun."

11
00:01:11.018 --> 00:01:16.363
The following year the third sister went deeper into the Upper World.

12
00:01:16.364 --> 00:01:23.548
"I swam up a river and saw rolling hills and woods filled with tall, green trees.

13
00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.739
I heard birds sing happy songs to their chicks.

14
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:33.681
In a small cove, humans were swimming—even without tails!"

15
00:01:33.682 --> 00:01:38.986
Frightened of the humans, the third sister fled back to the open sea.

16
00:01:38.987 --> 00:01:43.114
Hearing this, the fourth sister was less bold.

17
00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:48.569
She kept far away from land and stayed among the rough waves.

18
00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:54.992
"I saw playful dolphins jumping over each other above the water," she said to the others.

19
00:01:54.993 --> 00:01:59.519
"Huge whales spouted water through holes in their backs.

20
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.797
In the distance I saw ships.

21
00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:07.320
They were so far away that they looked like seagulls."

22
00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:10.669
Now the fifth sister had her turn.

23
00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:17.645
Her birthday was in winter, when the sea often turned a deep green and storms raged.

24
00:02:17.646 --> 00:02:22.531
Enormous icebergs stuck out of the water.

25
00:02:22.532 --> 00:02:30.303
"I sat in the snow on a mountain of ice, and I watched a ship sail by," she told her sisters.

26
00:02:30.304 --> 00:02:35.725
"Soon the sea became choppy and the green waves turned black.

27
00:02:35.726 --> 00:02:42.044
Thunder roared in my ears, and I saw lightning flash across the sky!"

28
00:02:42.045 --> 00:02:47.641
Some evenings the five older sisters swam to the surface together.

29
00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:51.228
They sat on rocks and sang to the ships.

30
00:02:51.229 --> 00:02:55.542
They had beautiful voices that rang through the air.

31
00:02:55.543 --> 00:03:01.159
But when the sailors heard the sisters' songs, they became frightened.

32
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.950
The sailors quickly turned their ships around to head for shore.

33
00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:11.612
As the years went by, humans told stories of the singing sisters.

34
00:03:11.613 --> 00:03:15.853
They said mermaids were wicked because they tricked humans.

35
00:03:15.854 --> 00:03:21.856
Foolish sailors loved to hear the mermaids' songs and would sail too close.

36
00:03:21.857 --> 00:03:25.536
Then their ships would crash into the rocks.

37
00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:28.267
None of these stories were true.

38
00:03:28.268 --> 00:03:31.460
The sisters did not want to hurt anyone.

39
00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:34.331
They just loved to sing!

40
00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:39.269
But the five mermaids eventually lost interest in the Upper World.

41
00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:44.002
And they spent less and less time singing to the ships.

42
00:03:44.003 --> 00:03:50.123
For the sea folk, there was no place as nice as their home at the bottom of the sea.

43
00:03:50.124 --> 00:03:56.229
The Sea Kingdom was the best place to live and always would be.

44
00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:01.566
For five years the Little Mermaid listened to her sisters' tales.

45
00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:06.029
She longed for her own adventure in the Upper World.

46
00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.586
"Oh, how I wish I were 15," she cried.

47
00:04:10.587 --> 00:04:21.310
"I know I will love the world up there and all the humans in it!"
